1
00:00:00,050 --> 00:00:03,312
How does a new merchant earn the right to take card payments?

2
00:00:03,362 --> 00:00:07,608
Picture a company that signs up on Monday and takes payments on Tuesday.

3
00:00:07,658 --> 00:00:11,496
Nobody saw its founding papers, or its director's passport.

4
00:00:11,546 --> 00:00:17,880
When complaints and disputed payments pile up, the bank cannot say who it signed with, or who let it in.

5
00:00:17,930 --> 00:00:22,440
To get a driving licence, you hand in your papers, and each one is checked.

6
00:00:22,490 --> 00:00:26,400
You get a licence with its own number, and every step goes in your file.

7
00:00:26,450 --> 00:00:29,208
A merchant earns its states the same way.

8
00:00:29,258 --> 00:00:31,080
Here is how it works.

9
00:00:31,130 --> 00:00:34,824
First, the merchant uploads its company documents.

10
00:00:34,874 --> 00:00:37,104
The bank must know who it does business with.

11
00:00:37,154 --> 00:00:38,976
This is know your business.

12
00:00:39,026 --> 00:00:41,448
Each file goes into the file store.

13
00:00:41,498 --> 00:00:46,848
The store reads each file's real type from the file's own contents, never from its name.

14
00:00:46,898 --> 00:00:51,120
So a file called "charter" that is really something else is refused.

15
00:00:51,170 --> 00:00:56,376
The store also keeps a checksum: a fingerprint worked out from every byte of the file.

16
00:00:56,426 --> 00:01:01,776
When the file is read back, its fingerprint must still match, so a changed file is caught.

17
00:01:01,826 --> 00:01:05,136
Next, a bank admin checks every document.

18
00:01:05,186 --> 00:01:10,080
Each one is verified, or rejected with a reason the merchant can read and fix.

19
00:01:10,130 --> 00:01:15,456
Only when every required document is verified can the company itself be verified.

20
00:01:15,506 --> 00:01:20,064
Then it signs a contract, and the contract carries its own unique number.

21
00:01:20,114 --> 00:01:22,392
No two merchants ever share one.

22
00:01:22,442 --> 00:01:28,224
Every move between states is written down: from where, to where, who, and why.

23
00:01:28,274 --> 00:01:34,176
That record is the status history, and it is written in the same step as the move itself.

24
00:01:34,226 --> 00:01:36,792
A move without its record cannot happen.

25
00:01:36,842 --> 00:01:38,664
Now watch the product.

26
00:01:38,714 --> 00:01:42,744
The viewer signs in as the merchant and opens Documents.

27
00:01:42,794 --> 00:01:48,768
The page says "Company documents", and explains that the bank checks who it works with before switching a merchant on.

28
00:01:48,818 --> 00:01:53,520
Two papers are marked Required: the company charter and the director's passport.

29
00:01:53,570 --> 00:01:57,672
Two more say "If it applies": a licence and a power of attorney.

30
00:01:57,722 --> 00:02:02,400
The viewer clicks Choose file, picks a sample charter, and clicks Upload.

31
00:02:02,450 --> 00:02:04,272
The page says "Uploaded.

32
00:02:04,322 --> 00:02:08,280
The bank will review it." The status reads "Waiting for review".

33
00:02:08,330 --> 00:02:10,152
Now the trick.

34
00:02:10,202 --> 00:02:15,648
The viewer uploads a file whose name says it is a document, but whose contents are something else.

35
00:02:15,698 --> 00:02:18,912
The picker lets it through, because it only looks at the name.

36
00:02:18,962 --> 00:02:21,792
The server reads the contents and refuses it.

37
00:02:21,842 --> 00:02:23,976
Next, the bank admin portal.

38
00:02:24,026 --> 00:02:27,072
The admin opens Merchants and picks this merchant.

39
00:02:27,122 --> 00:02:30,936
Each document has two buttons, Verify and Reject.

40
00:02:30,986 --> 00:02:35,304
Reject asks the admin to say what is wrong, so the merchant can fix it.

41
00:02:35,354 --> 00:02:37,200
The admin verifies both.

42
00:02:37,250 --> 00:02:44,424
If the merchant had not yet confirmed its email, the "Approve documents" button would stay grey, with a message saying so.

43
00:02:44,474 --> 00:02:48,768
Here the email is confirmed, so the admin clicks Approve documents.

44
00:02:48,818 --> 00:02:53,880
Then Sign contract, and types the contract number, as printed on the signed paper.

45
00:02:53,930 --> 00:02:56,424
Last, the admin opens History.

46
00:02:56,474 --> 00:03:01,176
Every move is there: from, to, who, and the reason.

47
00:03:01,226 --> 00:03:03,048
What does this protect?

48
00:03:03,098 --> 00:03:07,152
Without checked papers, the bank cannot say who it is paying.

49
00:03:07,202 --> 00:03:10,872
Without a fingerprint, a document could be swapped after it was checked.

50
00:03:10,922 --> 00:03:14,136
Without the history, nobody could say who approved what.

51
00:03:14,186 --> 00:03:18,624
Know your business protects the bank, the card network and every buyer.

52
00:03:18,674 --> 00:03:25,272
The status history protects the people who did the checking, because it shows exactly what they saw and when.

53
00:03:25,322 --> 00:03:30,936
So, like a driving licence: checked papers, a unique number, and every step in the file.

54
00:03:30,986 --> 00:03:34,032
Next: why switching a merchant on needs two people.
